# Build context is the repository ROOT (infra/docker/api.Dockerfile is built with `context: ../../`),
# so everything not excluded here is uploaded to the Docker daemon on every build.
#
# The first two entries are the ones that matter most. Without them a build on a deployment host
# would attempt to send the entire evidence volume — potentially tens of terabytes — to the daemon,
# and would then bake evidence content into an image layer where it could be extracted by anyone who
# can pull the image. That is a disclosure path, not just a slow build.

# ── Evidence and operator data: NEVER in a build context ──────────────────────
srv/
evidence/
*.evidence
backups/
*.restic
*.luks
models/
# Note: there is deliberately no `!models/.gitkeep` re-inclusion here. Once a parent directory is
# excluded, neither Docker nor git can re-include a path inside it, so writing one would be a
# comment that promises something the file does not do.

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets/
**/tls/

# ── Version control and CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# ── Python build artifacts and virtualenvs ────────────────────────────────────
.venv*/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ── Node / frontend build artifacts (the frontend image builds these itself) ──
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
.turbo/

# ── Documentation and tooling not needed at runtime ───────────────────────────
docs/
*.md
!backend/README.md
tools/

# ── Editor / OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
